/*  FUNCTION NAME:      COLNUM
    DESCRIPTION:*//**Returns the column number of an A1-style cell address passed as text. Like COLUMN() but accepts strings.*/
/*  RETURNS:            number: the column number of the address; lifts over arrays
    PARAMETERS:
        address         (Required) A1 address text (e.g. "AA17"), or an array/range of such. Any number of column letters ("XFE1", "ABCD9") and rows past 1048576. Sheet prefixes and $ anchors are ignored; for a range only its first cell is used. Text that is not an address returns TOPOS's "can't read" message. Result lifts element-wise.
    EXAMPLE:            =COLNUM("AA17") -> 27
    REVISIONS:          Date        Developer   Description
                        2026-05-20  Claude      Initial version
                        2026-11-06  Claude      Decode at the _mult constant via TOPOS (was a hard-coded 100000); any number of column letters, rows past 1048576; TOPOS's "can't read" message passes through instead of #N/A (#380)
                        2026-11-09  Claude      Help table removed from the formula; its text is the header metadata the argument hints read (#381, #382)
*/
COLNUM = LAMBDA(
//  Parameter Declarations
    [address],
    LET(
    //  Procedure
        pos, TOPOS(address),
        result, IF(ISNUMBER(pos), MOD(pos, _mult), pos),
        result
)
);
